# THE COMMITTED THIRD-PARTY LIBRARY BUILDS ARE VERBATIM ARTIFACTS.
#
# `src/lib/foundry/vendor/` holds five npm-published files -- React, ReactDOM,
# Babel standalone, Lucide and Tailwind -- committed so the platform can serve
# them to student bundles without fetching anything at build time. They are the
# published bytes and are not ours to reformat.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is `true` on this machine, so without this line git rewrites
# every LF in them to CRLF on checkout and back on commit. Measured: a stash and
# a pop changed the md5 of all five. That is not a correctness problem for the
# JavaScript, which runs either way, but it means the file we serve is no longer
# the file npm published, the byte counts stop matching the versions recorded in
# `src/lib/foundry/vendor.ts`, and the working tree can end up permanently dirty
# against its own committed blob.
#
# `-text` turns line-ending conversion off in both directions and keeps them
# byte-identical to the tarballs they came out of.
src/lib/foundry/vendor/*.js -text
